  "what_no_flip_means": "The gate did not close at ANY satellite count, including zero: the receiver kept reporting fix_type 3 throughout while satellites_visible tracked the commanded value down to 0. Two consequences. (1) WP-C6's `degraded` arm combined SIM_GPS_NUMSATS=4 with SIM_GPS_BYTELOSS=20 and attributed its closure to partial constellation loss. That attribution is WRONG: the satellite count contributes nothing, and the closure came from the byte loss, which is a receiver LINK failure. (2) In this generator the satellite count carried the entire injected fault while the gate, keyed on fix validity alone, saw nothing and the diagnosis stayed nominal. That is a routing failure demonstrated end to end: the signal was in the telemetry and the ingestion path does not read that field. It is ALSO a fidelity limit of this simulator, since a real receiver would not assert a 3D fix on zero satellites, and both readings must be reported.",
  "why": "WP-C6 asserted that fix-removing faults close the gate from two endpoints, 10 satellites and 0.17. This finds the flip point, which is the operational definition of which faults are self-occluding."
 }
}